"text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"itself, when it is a target, gives the trivial path first."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The sequence holds the graph (a value), so iterating again gives the same paths. The first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the rows the source reaches, O(n + m). A vertex that reaches no target is never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entered, but a partial path can still end where every way on is blocked by its own vertices,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the time between two paths is not bounded by a polynomial in n + m."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/traversal\/directedsimplepaths"]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every simple path of a directed graph from a source to any of a set of targets, lazily, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order a depth-first search from the source, taking out-edges in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" order, reaches them."}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Iterator"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/maxLength"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/makeIterator()"]},{"anchor":"Type-Aliases","title":"Type Aliases","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/DirectedSimplePaths\/Element"]},{"anchor":"Default-I